<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Has Iran modified its rocket systems to fire mines into the Strait of Hormuz?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b23621f2d5913b0660606db4734a5c13fd0fced23bb2f076ba914b0bfb57d7b5</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T05:57:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-has-iran-modified-its-rocket-systems-to-fire-mines-into-the-strait-of-hormuz--d9050c0ecfa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-has-iran-modified-its-rocket-systems-to-fire-mines-into-the-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">Fighting escalated in the Middle East over the weekend after US airstrikes on Sunday targeted Iranian rocket launchers on the island of Larak. The exchange of fire was instigated by the US in retaliation against Iran’s new capabilities for firing mines from rockets into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran’s use of rocket launchers to deploy sea mines into the strategic waterway would be unprecedented, but not implausible. Even so, some analysts remain sceptical.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Iran's army says it attacked US bases in Kuwait, UAE</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976ecaf97c152021ee720b547a65d83e8f10bebd8e56ed0b83655ace1b49f2bc</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T03:08:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran--67d09afbe2b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran" /><summary type="html">Iran's army on Thursday said it targeted US bases in the United Arab Emirates and Kuwait, despite US President Donald Trump threatening further strikes. This comes after extensive US bombardment on sites across Iran killed at least 19 people between Tuesday and Wednesday. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, US trade threats as Tehran blames Washington for wedding strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4226e5cd12960ab095dc3a867ad4004e19abe8fb77de8a842ee50958a44cbc01</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T01:22:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike--7495f90c90eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike" /><summary type="html">Iran and the United States traded threats on Wednesday after their heaviest military exchanges in weeks. Tehran accused Washington of striking a wedding party and called the attack a war crime. President Donald Trump threatened further US strikes, while Iran’s security chief warned Washington would face a “new strategy.”</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US-Iran war: Old videos falsely claim to show new attacks on American bases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5374938687be7ba398cc18b272966da4d1b83fb0018243b31554f9ee0aed8e23</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:57:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1--e29deba63932.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1" /><summary type="html">As US-Iran hostilities flare up and strikes resume, so has a wave of misinformation online. Old and unrelated videos are flooding social media, falsely presented as footage of new attacks. As tensions escalate, clips filmed in Dubai, Russia and the US have been misrepresented as Iranian strikes on US bases in the Gulf. Elsewhere, a 68-year-old video of a US nuclear test has been falsely claimed to show Iran detonating mines in the Strait of Hormuz. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli FM Gideon Sa'ar: 'I hope Iran will not make the mistake of attacking us'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:562af7af13541b3d4286f024d61dfc234e7a007c36774b579ea3ac154e493315</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:49:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us--4ec8673d7440.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israel's Minister of Foreign Affairs Gideon Sa’ar addressed the resumption in fighting between the US and Iran, and warned that any Iranian attack on Israel would trigger a "severe" response. He also accused Tehran of continuing to pursue "nuclear weapons aspirations", claiming that Israel "will not allow" Iran to achieve them.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Videos and debris raise questions over alleged US strike on Iranian wedding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6db856b05415a4dfc58f64045086cd8b7f72835de1a0ad222eeccfdac1d406c</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:31:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding--89b2ba4b7915.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding" /><summary type="html">On the evening of September 1, a barrage of US missile and drone attacks on a town in southern Iran allegedly struck a wedding ceremony, killing at least five people, including a four-year-old boy. FRANCE 24 geolocated a direct hit to the civilian building where local residents say the wedding was being held. The building was more than 135 meters from the apparent target, a communications tower.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel ‘organised and prepared’ to remove Gaza population if US gives green light, Katz says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c33f6236685d177eff99d24dcc958d1a14a4f7e53c82e6a511af5ae24de9bba</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:56:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-israel-organised-and-prepared-to-remove-gaza-population-if-us-gives-green-light-katz--8521b89aab45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-israel-organised-and-prepared-to-remove-gaza-population-if-us-gives-green-light-katz" /><summary type="html">Israel is "organised and prepared" to remove Palestininians from Gaza "by every way possible", Defence Minister Israel Katz told reporters Wednesday, adding that there was no alternative "solution" to crisis. The Israeli government was simply waiting for the US to figure out where to take the displaced Gazans, he said.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Xi calls on Mideast nations to be ‘masters of their own affairs’ in rare Egypt visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24906c53ca5d0c906c596fd9ec278bc33439d1edcd3d052b7a90cbdc4b35b419</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:22:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-xi-calls-on-mideast-nations-to-be-masters-of-their-own-affairs-in-rare-egypt-visit--a27043953780.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-xi-calls-on-mideast-nations-to-be-masters-of-their-own-affairs-in-rare-egypt-visit" /><summary type="html">Chinese President Xi Jinping on Wednesday called on "the people of the Middle East" to oppose "externalinterference" and consider reshaping the region's security order during a visit to Egypt. The rare visit by the Chinese leader comes as Beijing aims to expand its influence in the region as the Iran war tests the reliability of the traditional US security umbrella in a vital geostrategic zone.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UNIFIL peacekeepers patrol south Lebanon, caught between Israel and Hezbollah</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a17dbd4d34941cfbb4475bc8c6b1d14c14abf71913c32442f2a950e9c87499</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:41:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260902-unifil-peacekeepers-patrol-south-lebanon-caught-between-israel-and-hezbollah--b0682915af5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260902-unifil-peacekeepers-patrol-south-lebanon-caught-between-israel-and-hezbollah" /><summary type="html">Since this spring, about 6 percent of Lebanon has been occupied by the Israeli army. On the ground, around 600 French soldiers from the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) continue to patrol the zone. The delicate peacekeeping mission documents violations of UN resolutions by both Israel and Hezbollah, with its own future highly uncertain. Our France 2 colleagues report, with FRANCE 24's Florent Marchais.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: US accused of hitting wedding party in latest strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fca6a3ee525ac3e7cfa91d2e6182855ec395403142efb6c02f90a2f751ab8b4</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T11:11:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-iran-us-accused-of-hitting-wedding-party-in-latest-strikes--5e3776f2d927.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-iran-us-accused-of-hitting-wedding-party-in-latest-strikes" /><summary type="html">#Tehran says at least four people were killed and dozens more wounded in a #US strike on a town near in the south of #Iran, near the Strait of #Hormuz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says prepared to resume strikes on Iran at 'any time'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4eab5d3c57a340b85bfae0c59744a88c19227f651a64416927125e2d699a1ea</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T01:38:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-us-military-striking-targets-in-iran-after-attempted-attacks-on-shipping--2a2323f6d3bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-us-military-striking-targets-in-iran-after-attempted-attacks-on-shipping" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Wednesday suggested he was ready to strike Iran again “at any time" after he proposed renaming the Strait of Hormuz the “Trump Strait.” Earlier, Iran had attacked US military bases in the Gulf following another round of US airstrikes on Iranian soil. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US and Iran trade fire as hostilities flare again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8635a20c88285199abc106ecadf855ca65efff29778e083c0e48fc10c51fbfc</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:15:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-us-and-iran-trade-fire-as-hostilities-flare-again--37e010d049e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-us-and-iran-trade-fire-as-hostilities-flare-again" /><summary type="html">The US military hit targets in Iran on Tuesday as Tehran reponded with retaliatory strikes as hostilities between the two countries flared once again in an intermittent war that has lasted more than six months. One US strike hit a home hosting a wedding, killing four people and wounding dozens, local officials said.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>A Hezbollah hideout stuffed with cash? Nope, this video was AI-generated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72d5630caffda638af8571a60468dda7386edf11b9d1c37ac27666879535e85b</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:01:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-hezbollah-hideout-stuffed-cash-ai-generated--9c252e98ffac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-hezbollah-hideout-stuffed-cash-ai-generated" /><summary type="html">A number of pro-Israel social media accounts have shared a video they claim shows wads of cash and stacks of gold bars in a cache belonging to a deceased Hezbollah leader. There's only one issue: the footage was created using AI. The original video was shared by an Egyptian satirical site.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu's wife shares conspiracy claim that opposition leader knew of Oct 7 attacks in advance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fbe1d51cb5eaebc7c211bd383e0143d419ed6561f3ad146af4c43f215e50dd2</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:36:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-netanyahu-s-wife-shares-conspiracy-that-opposition-leader-had-early-knowledge-of-oct-7-atta--a964727714fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-netanyahu-s-wife-shares-conspiracy-that-opposition-leader-had-early-knowledge-of-oct-7-attacks" /><summary type="html">As Israel prepares for what are expected to be close-fought parliamentary elections in October, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's wife Sara on Monday shared a conspiracy theory that centre-left opposition figure Yair Golan had advance warning of the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US military striking targets in Iran after attempted attacks on shipping</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e9ec657983fa00dbcd976b1d046b0797ef4ef607ca2185f4cc4e8c85a84561b</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T03:38:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-middle-east-live-oil-prices-extend-gains-as-us-iran-tensions-flare-again--805a2484da57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-middle-east-live-oil-prices-extend-gains-as-us-iran-tensions-flare-again" /><summary type="html">The US military said on Tuesday it is striking new targets in Iran as hostilities flare again after a month without military action. US Central Command said that the strikes follow recent attempted attacks by the Iranian government against commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens to ‘hit Iran hard’ as strikes resume after month-long lull</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c17b672b518187c844e017b262f2a61fc4bfb0a712e3c22221bf2d9972e54ea</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T20:36:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull--926c2ca9c70e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said Monday that the US would hit back against Iranian attacks on US targets in the Middle East, according to a Fox News reporter. The Iranian attacks were themselves a response to US strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first flare-up in a month.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump vows to hit back 'hard' after first exchange of fire with Iran in weeks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47c8bf7c4ac6f7736c2333f270d379cbfeea0e1875f2581937bbeeac116eadac</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T18:37:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks--7701c0e7ac56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump threatened to hit Iran "hard" after the two foes traded fire for the first time in over a month, while Iran's president warned that more fighting with the US was not in his country's interest. After six months of war, the foes remain at an impasse, with Iran keeping the strategic Strait of Hormuz closed and the US persisting with a naval counter-blockade of Iran. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>Raising the Altalena: Netanyahu digs up sunken 1948 arms ship in ‘pre-election stunt’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e57bdb4731ce3eba1cab67e6854715a53365a92a25422cc52ba6d1d8224db785</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T16:54:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt--b62ae1447324.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt" /><summary type="html">A ship carrying arms for a right-wing militia, the Altalena was sunk 78 years ago off the coast of Tel Aviv at the orders of Israel’s founders. The discovery of its wreckage last week has given the country’s right-wing government ammunition to target the left and attempt to redirect the campaign for legislative elections in October.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Latest flare-up between US and Iran bring conflict's lull to an end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e72b6d549489ed9bf56347cd1f540188e50b2e0497210bdd99b8828bf57b8b71</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:33:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end--9f77617ac27c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end" /><summary type="html">Iran's foreign minister has accused Israel's Benjamin Netanyahu of tricking the United States into war with the Islamic Republic. Over six months into the conflict, there appears to be no end in sight. This after the US struck sites in Iran, prompting Tehran to respond. An April ceasefire brought an end to intense fighting, but sporadic attacks have continued over the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran's closure of the waterway during the conflict has pressured global oil markets, and in turn Donald Trump at home.</summary></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz accessibility at the centre of US-Iran war flare-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9591061c105dc782f5897058740df697de31af1cfeea537398901c8505e4c119</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:47:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-accessibility-at-the-centre-of-us-iran-war-flare-up--9de5d0383172.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-accessibility-at-the-centre-of-us-iran-war-flare-up" /><summary type="html">For the first time in a month, the US has launched strikes against Iran. The attack targeted the shipping island of Larak in the Strait of Hormuz. The US says it was aimed at preventing Tehran from placing sea mines in the strategic shipping lane, just days after Washington announced it had completed clearing explosives from there. Iran then reiterated its attacks, saying it had struck two US military bases in Jordan. FRANCE 24's Rochelle Ferguson-Bouyahi tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Relentless heat worsens Gaza's ongoing struggle to access water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c61c5cebc2966400070d40a5962eefb8e6a0498ca56827e34c5c0389cb42233</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:49:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/relentless-heat-worsens-gaza-s-ongoing-struggle-to-access-water--85e6fae055ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/relentless-heat-worsens-gaza-s-ongoing-struggle-to-access-water" /><summary type="html">In Gaza, securing drinking water is a relentless daily struggle. The war with Israel has destroyed critical water and sanitation infrastructure, and as temperatures soar, the extreme heat is escalating an already severe shortage into a deadly humanitarian crisis. Two and a half years of war with Israel have damaged or destroyed nearly 90% of Gaza’s water and sanitation infrastructure according to UNICEF.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran, US trade fire in first exchange in a month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91b0c84526e42d44ae29198cb1d7ab7b7bee3ea2e79f8793e20c57eb1145b1d9</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:49:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-iran-us-trade-fire-in-first-exchange-in-a-month--237ef98b8b75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-iran-us-trade-fire-in-first-exchange-in-a-month" /><summary type="html">Iran attacked US military targets in the Middle East on Monday in retaliation following American strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first exchange of fire for a month in a war that has engulfed the region.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East war flares up after Iran responds to US attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2226520fcdd2dcf3deaa92a495b6d3b0e886d8302cec3940de8741ed27a255c</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:43:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-war-flares-up-after-iran-responds-to-us-attacks--d008a7b9fca7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-war-flares-up-after-iran-responds-to-us-attacks" /><summary type="html">Iran attacked US military targets in the Middle East in retaliation for the first American strikes on its territory in a month. This signs a fresh flare-up of the war that has engulfed the region. Washington said its attacks were aimed at preventing Iran from placing more sea mines in the strait and as it threatens new secondary economic sanctions. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah is in Tehran and tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US renews attack on Iran while threatening financial sanctions on Tehran allies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa71496c6ba2a00613342b2e4738dd05a0e5af91f469d5817448ed9fbe7d6ff8</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:40:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-renews-attack-on-iran-while-threatening-financial-sanctions-on-tehran-allies--8d1a4f56eab1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-renews-attack-on-iran-while-threatening-financial-sanctions-on-tehran-allies" /><summary type="html">Hostilities between the US and Iran resumed after a month's pause. The US said Iran was preparing to launch sea mines into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran retaliated by hitting US military bases in Jordan. Meanwhile, the US Treasury Secretary said there would be more economic sanctions on the way for banks doing business with Iran.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran says continuing war ‘not in our interest’ after fighting flares</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7798eb42f1e95b36dd3393d8f4c5b9964f182c9e83aab9b222db7cfa034d556e</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T23:02:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month--572426b25307.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian said Monday that continuing the war with the United States was not in his country's interest, following a fresh military flare-up between the two countries after a month-long lull. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US forces strike Iranian launchers on Larak island in Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74092eb25b59c198efbaefe4cf6da07cf18abced9cece9cab2f56476de31d96c</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T20:27:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz--1eaea36d941e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in the first military action in a month, a US official said Sunday. ⁠Iran's ⁠Revolutionary ​Guards ​said the attack on Larak ​island ‌killed and wounded ⁠several Iranian fighters and ​civilians, and ‌vowed to punish those ​responsible.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu condemns violence in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc97542ccc1d8e586a2a1ba963d1bf3fd130723c0e37a9fbbbbccaed99b2b862</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:46:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank--f146c0bf0b9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">It was a rare condemnation from what is widely seen as the most religious and ultranationalist government in Israel’s history. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu condemned recent attacks by Israeli settlers on Palestinians in the occupied West Bank, but described the violence as the actions of a “handful of rioters.” Tensions have surged across the territory, with activists accusing settlers of acting with impunity. Much of the recent violence has taken place in the town of Qusra. Peter O’Brien reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu condemns 'criminal acts of violence' by settlers in West Bank villages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:348364db68f0f9b34fc60e3125a60992e3eac99862821e0cd1deb99f5cd89cae</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T18:34:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260829-netanyahu-condemns-criminal-acts-of-violence-by-settlers-in-west-bank-villages--94a13b44b42b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260829-netanyahu-condemns-criminal-acts-of-violence-by-settlers-in-west-bank-villages" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday condemned what he called "criminal acts of violence" perpetrated by Israeli settlers in two Palestinian villages. Earlier in August, a group of settlers blocked supplies from entering Palestinian houses on the outskirts of Qusra and attacked a Palestinian family and a foreign media crew in nearby Jalud.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war reaches 6-month mark: Conflict cost $1,100 per US taxpayer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a4922d40e09c8b3d26390b420be9af073f405a7eeb5c32f0d3ebb4f4538ec54</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T15:24:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-war-reaches-6-month-mark-conflict-cost-1-100-per-us-taxpayer--0914f5e1ed99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-war-reaches-6-month-mark-conflict-cost-1-100-per-us-taxpayer" /><summary type="html">After six months of war, Iran’s leadership has coalesced around a hard core of military generals and clerics long entrenched in the ruling theocracy. They are ready for a potentially long confrontation with the US and determined to prevent any unrest at home. It’s a far cry from US President Donald Trump’s initial hopes of toppling the Islamic Republic and his subsequent claims that “regime change” had brought more compromising officials to the fore. In an analysis, FRANCE 24's Philip Turle said the war had so far cost around 1,100 US dollars for each US taxpayer.</summary></entry><entry><title>Situation in Niger 'not stabilised yet' as security forces deploy around airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bea67327cf9280d51b5cd021631209eaf33acc6941f6b2f23f334f6e0c0cddd</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:39Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T13:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/situation-in-niger-not-stabilised-yet-as-security-forces-deploy-around-airport--ef7479b2be5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/situation-in-niger-not-stabilised-yet-as-security-forces-deploy-around-airport" /><summary type="html">A group of soldiers in Niger rebelled against officers at a key military base and fired at sensitive locations in the capital, Niamey, in an apparent mutiny marked by gunfire and explosions, authorities said Saturday, in what was seen as a major threat to the country's struggling junta. FRANCE 24's Wassim Nasr brings you this analysis.</summary></entry></feed>
